# The production image's build context (Dockerfile, ADR-0015) is an allowlist: everything is
# excluded, then only what the image needs is re-included, so a new or stray file (a secret, test
# output, a local build) can never slip into the build by accident.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.nvmrc
!e2e/package.json
!apps/shell/
!services/api/

# Excluded again inside the re-included directories.
**/node_modules
**/.env*
**/*.map
**/.DS_Store
**/*:Zone.Identifier
apps/shell/dist
apps/shell/coverage
services/api/config/master.key
services/api/config/credentials.yml.enc
services/api/config/credentials/
services/api/log/*
services/api/tmp/*
services/api/storage/*
services/api/spec
services/api/docs
services/api/coverage
services/api/.bundle
services/api/vendor/bundle
